 transplantation: contraindication vs risk</article-title><source>American Journal of Transplantation</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>1488</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14629279</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koka</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Chia</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Terasaki</surname><given-names>PI</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Chia</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozawa</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The role of IgA anti-HLA class I antibodies in kidney transplant survival</article-title><source>Transplantation</source><year>1993</year><volume>56</volume><fpage>207</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8333044</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mao</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Terasaki</surname><given-names>PI</given-names></name><name><surname>Cai</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Briley</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Catrou</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Haisch</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Extremely high association between appearance of HLA antibodies and failure of kidney grafts in a five-year longitudinal study</article-title><source>American Journal of Transplantation</source><year>2007</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>864</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17391129</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Terasaki</surname><given-nam